  "question": {
    "html": "<p>In an experiment on Planet X, a small sphere of radius <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"1.0\\; \\textup{m}\"></span> and mass <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"3.0\\; \\textup{kg}\"></span> is made to roll without slipping on a horizontal surface with an angular speed of <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"5.0\\; \\textup{rad\\,s}^{-1}\"></span>. Then a ramp is placed in the path of the sphere and the sphere rolls up the ramp without slipping.</p>\n\n<figure data-asset-id=\"fig_01\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 1\" src=\"asset:fig_01\"/></figure>\n\n<p>The maximum vertical height reached by the centre of the sphere is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"4.5\\; \\textup{m}\"></span>. The moment of inertia for the sphere is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"I = \\frac{2}{5}mr^{2}\"></span>, where <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"m\"></span> is the mass and <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"r\"></span> is the radius of the sphere.</p>\n<p>What is the weight of the sphere on Planet X?</p>\n<p></p>\n<ol class=\"mcq-options\">\n<li data-label=\"A\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"9.0\\; \\textup{N}\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"B\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"12\\; \\textup{N}\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"C\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"15\\; \\textup{N}\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"D\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"18\\; \\textup{N}\"></span></li>\n</ol>"
  },
